"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_

**Don't emit blobs your own deserializer will reject.**

`deserializeVaultBlobV2()` now rejects `key_len === 0`, but `serializeVaultBlobV2()` can still produce that payload. That makes the public API internally inconsistent and breaks round-tripping for callers that accidentally pass an empty wrapped key.



<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
 export function serializeVaultBlobV2(
   encryptedRootFolderKey: Uint8Array,
   encryptedMetadataJson: Uint8Array
 ): Uint8Array {
   const keyLen = encryptedRootFolderKey.length;
+  if (keyLen === 0) {
+    throw new Error('Encrypted key too short for v2 blob (must be > 0 bytes)');
+  }
   if (keyLen > 0xffff) {
     throw new Error(`Encrypted key too long for v2 blob (${keyLen} bytes, max ${0xffff})`);
   }
```
</details>

<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

